# Never COPY host artifacts into the build context. In particular:
#
# - node_modules — the deps stage installs the correct pinned versions
#   inside the image; if this dir is present on the host it gets copied
#   over the fresh install by `COPY . .` and the built bundle then ships
#   whatever the host happened to have. That's how a bumped
#   package-lock.json can appear to build successfully with npm ci
#   inside deps stage but the runner ends up bundled against stale
#   client code from the host. Learned the hard way during the Aegis
#   phase-3 rollout on 2026-07-22 (v20 through v22 all shipped the
#   pre-phase-3 JS client despite the lockfile bump).
#
# - .next / build outputs — must be produced by the builder stage,
#   never seeded from the host (turbopack/next caches from a different
#   node/turbopack version corrupt the build in confusing ways).
node_modules
.next
out

# Local envs — the runtime container reads its config from /api/config
# and .env-gatekeeper*; the .env.local on the dev host must not ship.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# VCS + editor + OS clutter.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs / scripts that don't belong in the runtime image.
LICENSE
README.md
build-publish.sh
VERSION
docker-compose.example.yaml
NGINX_CONF_SKILL.md
